{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqgzmvnkaqy","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Pluggable agentic-CLI LLM backend (Claude then Codex then Cursor), dashboard-selectable, hard-block when none configured","summary":"DESIGN direction for the new follow-up. Reframe: the LLM CLI is zonoid's REQUIRED engine (judging, learning, labeling all need it), not an opt-in feature. Make it a PLUGGABLE backend selectable from the dashboard. Two decisions taken: (1) Phase 1 supports AGENTIC-CLI backends only — the spawn-a-self-driving-agent model used today (claude -p that reasons and calls back to the daemon over HTTP/MCP): Claude first (refactor the current hardcoded path into the first provider), then Codex, then Cursor; each provider is just different argv plus auth on the same model. Raw-API and OpenRouter (a daemon-driven judge loop, a different execution model) are DEFERRED to phase 2. (2) HARD-BLOCK when no valid backend: if no backend is configured, or the selected provider is not installed/authenticated, the engine refuses to run drains/judging and surfaces a clear setup error directing the user to configure a backend in the dashboard; the ORCH_HEADLESS_DRAINS flag is effectively replaced by 'is a valid backend configured and authed'. ARCHITECTURE: new lib/llm-backend.js adapter interface plus provider registry, each provider implementing resolveBin / isAvailable / isAuthed / buildInvocation / parseResult; generalize lib/claude-cli.js into the Claude provider; route lib/headless-drain.js and the inner onboard-learn spawn through the SELECTED backend instead of hardcoded claude; config in overlay.config.backend (provider + model), persisted, read/written via a GET and POST /config/backend daemon endpoint; dashboard settings panel showing each provider's detected install and auth status with an active-provider selector. This FOLDS the installer task 4b12fe1f-4bef-4c82-908d-0f07f56f3638/10 (its Claude-CLI detection becomes multi-backend detect/select; the .mcp.json env-merge fix stays valid; the --headless-drains opt-in becomes a --backend flag plus dashboard config). The windowsHide task /9 is independent and stays. NOT YET BUILT: a sustained Anthropic API overload currently blocks sub","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-16T18:41:03.680Z","vec":[-0.10690979659557343,-0.0017999517731368542,-0.08922792226076126,-0.041584860533475876,0.048907097429037094,-0.030661258846521378,-0.010272960178554058,0.07388213276863098,-0.024757515639066696,0.014430778101086617,0.04286767169833183,-0.009943134151399136,0.0676165372133255,-0.035043083131313324,-0.004600652493536472,0.03980999439954758,0.06935792416334152,-0.02159777097404003,-0.010699136182665825,-0.005653231404721737,0.04190859571099281,-0.023553326725959778,-0.0023840670473873615,-0.008889562450349331,-0.1096782460808754,-0.03962276503443718,-0.047297511249780655,0.000131705601233989,-0.02046959474682808,-0.05154707282781601,0.029345722869038582,0.08638866990804672,-0.11590000987052917,-0.0534600205719471,0.0033447067253291607,0.07250397652387619,0.011243367567658424,-0.04071241617202759,-0.0877605751156807,-0.0264869574457407,0.07976926863193512,0.06663913279771805,-0.06573022902011871,-0.04016820341348648,0.01693119667470455,-0.09841477870941162,-0.05226745456457138,-0.02558843232691288,-0.037097200751304626,-0.06047748401761055,-0.05494305118918419,-0.003298545954748988,0.012921692803502083,0.017215179279446602,0.0035077109932899475,0.07150442898273468,-0.041782401502132416,0.05355314165353775,0.0028505101799964905,-0.010195777751505375,0.004625376779586077,-0.04312894493341446,-0.005920051131397486,0.00847709272056818,0.011705410666763783,0.004336748272180557,-0.06368506699800491,-0.05228433758020401,0.02732091024518013,-0.039456967264413834,-0.029775474220514297,-0.02576880343258381,-0.06018294021487236,-0.0925227701663971,0.004409324377775192,0.021254966035485268,-0.0055224960669875145,0.07910982519388199,-0.022440696135163307,-0.1744883954524994,-0.01252725999802351,0.032936267